417] [17592186573913 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573913 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y,z)=12{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2},$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573913 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b089fead-c3aa-5630-9094-3b342b5bd931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573913 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=12.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ 12{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{z}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=12$ is the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{z}^{2}=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{z}{y-x}$ that passes through the point $P(2,1,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4d46c54-bc24-5068-beab-fa23fb4611cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573945 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1,3) & =\\frac{z}{y-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{z}{y-x} & =-3 \\\\ z & =-3(y-x) \\\\ z & =3x-3y \\\\ 3x-3y-z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(2,1,3)$ is the plane $3x-3y-z=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
